      <div type="clause" n="46">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 46</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="518" ed="#liebermann"/>Nus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.13"/> ne semble pas raisoun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.14"/>, que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.15"/> l’um<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.5"/> face pruvance, sur testimonie ki conussent ço que entercé<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.16"/> est; e que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.15"/> nul nel prust devant le terme de VI meis, aprés iço<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.17"/> que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.15"/> l’aveir [f]u<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.18"/> emblé.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="518" ed="#liebermann"/>Ne probacio fiat super testes. Absonum uidetur et iuri contrarium, ut probacio fiat, super testes qui rem calumpniatam cognoscunt; nec admittatur probacio ante terminum statutum, scilicet VI. mensem, ex quo furatum fuit quod calumpniatur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="46" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="272" ed="#robertson"/>Nus ne semble pas raisoun que l'um face pruvance sur testimonie ki conussent ço que entercé est, e que nul nel prust devant le terme de VI meis aprés iço que l'aveir [f]u emblé.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="518" ed="#liebermann"/>46. Uns dünkt kein Recht, dass jemand Beweiseid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#LeisWl_46.lnote.de1.c"/> leisten dürfe, [siegend<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#LeisWl_46.lnote.de1.d"/>] über Zeugenschaft [der Nachbarn des Bestohlenen], die das Angeschlagene kennen; und niemand [also fortan] dürfe es beweisen vor der Frist von 6 Monaten, nachdem das Vieh gestohlen ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">46. It seems to us no right that someone should be allowed to give an oath of proof, [prevailing] over testimony [of the neighbours of the man robbed] who know the attached thing; and let no one [therefore henceforth] be allowed to prove it before the term of 6 months after the cattle was stolen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="273" ed="#robertson"/>We regard it as unjust that a man should claim ownership against the witness of those who recognise the thing vouched to warranty. No-one shall claim ownership in less than six months from the time that the livestock was stolen.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="518"><ref target="clause:IICn_24-3">II Cn 24.3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 24, 3</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 272–273 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 518, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">lun <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lun Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XLIV. <hi rend="italic">I;</hi> Aus <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XLIV. I; Aus Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-son Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qui <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qui Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">entre <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">entre Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">co <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">co Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_46.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">su <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">su I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_46.lnote.de1.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">das bei ihm Beanspruchte sei von seiner eigenen Zucht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">that what is claimed in his possession is of his own rearing</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_46.lnote.de1.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sour: <hi rend="italic">gegen</hi> (<hi rend="italic">Godefroy</hi>); ‘supérieur au témoignage’; <hi rend="italic">Chevallet. Nicht</hi> ‘durch Zeugen’.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sour: against (Godefroy); ‘supérieur au témoignage’; Chevallet. Not ‘through witnesses’.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_46.lnote.de._" n="-" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd</hi>. 25e</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid</hi>. 25e</seg></note>
      </div>
